	Raytracing
		foreach pixel, foreach triangle, find closest intersection

		how intersect triangle and ray?

		given: O, r, t, v0, v1, v2
			P = O + rt
			P = v0 + (v1 - v0) * b + (v2 - v0) * c
			  = v0 * (1 - b - c) + v1 * b + v2 * c
			   => a = 1 - b - c

			O + rt = v0 + (v1 - v0) * b + (v2 - v0) * c
				knowns: O, r, v0, v1, v2
				unknowns: t, b, c

			let M = <v0, v1, v2> the matrix where its columns are v0, v1, v2
			               column vector
			O + rt = M * (1 - b - c, b, c)

			(1 - b - c, b, c) = M^-1 * O + M^-1 * r * t

			let Q0 = M^-1 * O
			let Q1 = M^-1 * r

			1 = (Q0x + Q0y + Q0z) + t * (Q1x + Q1y + Q1z)
				and solve for t

			if a >= 0 && b >= 0 && c >= 0
				then inside triangle
				and can use weights to blend parameters (color, normal, tex coords)


